================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover every file in this repository: the Python package
under src/voxelmill/, the C++ sources under native/, the build and measurement
scripts under scripts/, the documentation under docs/, the schemas, the icon
artwork under icons/ and packaging/, and the test fixtures under fixtures/.
All of it is original work by the copyright holder above. No third-party source
code is vendored into this repository.

This license does NOT cover the third-party libraries that VoxelMill depends
on, links against, or bundles into a distributable AppImage. Those keep their
own licenses. Every one of them is inventoried, with its license text and any
obligation it places on a redistributor, in:

    licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md

None of those dependencies is copyleft in a way that conflicts with MIT. The
LGPL components (Qt via PySide6, and the system C/C++ runtimes) are used
through dynamic linking only, which imposes notice and relinking obligations on
a binary distribution but places no condition on this source code. Those
obligations, and how the AppImage build satisfies them, are set out in
licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md under "AppImage distribution obligations".

================================================================================
FILE FORMAT INTEROPERABILITY
================================================================================

VoxelMill reads and writes the ELEGOO GOO and CHITUBOX CTB slice formats, and
speaks the SDCP printer protocol. These implementations are original, written
from published format specifications and verified against reference files; see
docs/goo-format.md for the sources, revisions and verification method. File
formats and protocols are not themselves subject to copyright, and no code was
taken from any other implementation of them.

ELEGOO, CHITUBOX, Mars, Sunlu and Jayo are trademarks of their respective
owners. VoxelMill is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of
them. Those names appear here only to identify the hardware, materials and
formats VoxelMill interoperates with.
